  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather through next Thursday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nStrong Noreaster has passed well to the southeast of our area \nand will continue to bring brisk winds to the area this\nafternoon. Temps likely to remain in the 40s for most locations\ntoday. \n\nA prolonged period of dry weather continue through the weekend\nwith the next cold front moving through Monday. Front will\nlikely be moisture-starved as the one that moved through yda.\nTemps following fropa will be chilly on Tuesday and Wednesday as\nCanadian high pressure builds in. The prolonged dry spell is \nvery likely to persist into Thursday of next week.",
